3.2 pop_checks
==============

‘pop_checks’ is a list of checks that validate expected responses and
behaviours from the services in the scenario.  These checks help verify
that the services return valid and expected data before proceeding with
the scenario execution.

   A check is defined by:

   ‘check_url’ (required, string) – The endpoint path to be tested
within the service.  This should be a relative path, such as
"/api/v1/forecast", which will be appended to the base_url of the
service.

   ‘service_id’ (required, string) – A reference to the id of the
service being checked.  This links the check to a specific service
defined in pop_services.

   ‘json_body_patterns’ (optional, list of objects) – A list of
conditions that must be met within the JSON response body.  Each pattern
defines a JSON field to inspect and a condition that must be satisfied.

   Each json_body_patterns entry includes:

   ‘pattern’ (required, string) – A JSON path-like expression that
identifies the field in the response body.  This uses the Rust ‘jql’
library.

   ‘condition’ (required, string) – A logical condition to be checked.

   Supported conditions include:

   ‘!= ""’ (ensures the field is not empty) ‘== ""’ (ensures the field
is empty) ‘> 0’ (ensures the field is greater than zero) ‘>= 0’ (ensures
the field is non-negative) ‘< 0’ (ensures the field is smaller than
zero) ‘<= 0’ (ensures the field is non-positive)


